\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Nearer, my God, to Thee,
\par Nearer to Thee!
\par E'en though it be a cross
\par That raiseth me,
\par Still all my song shall be,
\par Nearer, my God, to Thee,
\par Nearer to Thee
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Though, like the wanderer,
\par The sun gone down,
\par Darkness be over me,
\par My rest a stone,
\par Yet in my dreams I'd be
\par Nearer, my God, to Thee,
\par Nearer to Thee!
\par \pard\fi720 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There let the way appear,
\par Steps unto heaven;
\par All that Thou send'st to me
\par In mercy given;
\par Angels to beckon me
\par Nearer, my God, to Thee,
\par Nearer to Thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then with my waking thoughts
\par Bright with Thy praise,
\par Out of my stony griefs
\par Bethel I'll raise;
\par So by my woes to be
\par Nearer, my God, to Thee,
\par Nearer to Thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Or if on joyful wing
\par Cleaving the sky,
\par Sun, moon, and stars forgot,
\par Upwards I fly,
\par Still all my song shall be,
\par Nearer, my God, to Thee,
\par Nearer to Thee!
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f2 
\par }

